{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"38103db9136b6745c676b097bfe424cc1ae0719e7cde71c45bb76b1fd5db2b58","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_da030ef5e56f3b0d8b5a26c0c490315c1bc9dd473950b8c7d62bd64f083c9b6e","overall_assessment":"The paper is generally well-organized and clearly written, with a logical flow from motivation to method and experiments. The mathematical notation is consistent and the derivations are well-explained. The main clarity weakness lies in the presentation of the algorithm, where the stochastic corruption process is described in text and equations but lacks a concise pseudocode block, which would improve reproducibility. The figures and tables are adequately described in the text, though the caption for Figure 1 is somewhat generic.","paper_id":"B1Igu2ogg","paper_identity_sha256":"61c36d5dd24425b835639f62e155c1f49b1de775cbddad8be0397a1ea8006e56","prompt_identity_sha256":"2a7ec7ad32a2a1500b1d7d4ac7ec157fbd08e876328881145af480111814cd4f","raw_response_sha256":"45df8dc8ee12c9a04d6e01f945fd8089a5eabb93603b29ea702943fe7f237d35","request_identity_sha256":"4c755b6f7fe5f30f8384e7914e417019cfd2207038a9f25364b35dca2c036d80","reviewer_identity_sha256":"32b29c26fbf1508e066dfb25b1a9a3fe0654c5869a7da3020e1e8e61940befe3","role":"CLAR","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"5437ae772fd01d90cdce9afe503559c28ca64d281d16679be3fc84e0a0b26961","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-005","SRC-013","SRC-014"],"review_text":"The paper is well-structured, with a clear progression from the introduction of the problem to the proposed method and experimental validation. The terminology is precise, and key concepts such as 'corruption model' and 'data-dependent regularization' are clearly defined and consistently used. The narrative is smooth, and the prose is concise and readable. However, the presentation of the algorithm could be improved by including a pseudocode block that summarizes the training and testing procedures. Currently, the stochastic process for generating the global context is described in text and equations (e.g., Eq. 1), but a step-by-step algorithmic description would make it easier for readers to implement the method. This would enhance the self-containedness of the algorithm presentation and aid in reproducibility.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-WRT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-007","SRC-013","SRC-016","SRC-018"],"review_text":"The mathematical notation is consistent and well-defined. The paper introduces all necessary symbols in Section 2, and these are used consistently throughout the method and experiments sections. The derivations, particularly the Taylor expansion and the resulting regularization term, are clearly explained and well-motivated. The use of overbraces in Eq. 2 to label the local and global context terms is a helpful visual aid. The notation for the corruption process (Eq. 1) is clear, and the subsequent derivation of the Hessian and variance matrices is logically presented. There are no significant inconsistencies or missing definitions in the mathematical exposition.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-NOT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-011","SRC-023","SRC-027","SRC-032","SRC-034"],"review_text":"The figures and tables are adequately described in the text. The caption for Figure 1 is brief but sufficient to identify the model architecture. The text provides a detailed description of the figure, explaining the roles of the local and global context. The tables (e.g., Table 1, Table 2, Table 4, Table 5) are clearly formatted and contain all necessary information for interpreting the results. The captions for the tables are descriptive and provide context for the data presented. The textual descriptions of the t-SNE visualizations (Figures 2 and 3) are detailed and help the reader understand the clustering of document representations. However, the caption for Figure 1 could be more specific, mentioning the key components of the model (e.g., input layer, projection layer, output layer) to make it more informative on its own.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-FIG"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"5cc19d81985964a6399730c5f0b58610d1fd3dc3dd9a982a6e47bae5ee7fe29d","paper_id":"B1Igu2ogg","paper_ordinal":7,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"45df8dc8ee12c9a04d6e01f945fd8089a5eabb93603b29ea702943fe7f237d35","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"B1Igu2ogg","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"702a49c1468a5648c5261061380f4e22b5da6728cd67d81ede62c8e309850cf5","request_identity_sha256":"4c755b6f7fe5f30f8384e7914e417019cfd2207038a9f25364b35dca2c036d80","role":"CLAR","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v6","usage":{"completion_tokens":806,"prompt_tokens":19958,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":20764},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"4c755b6f7fe5f30f8384e7914e417019cfd2207038a9f25364b35dca2c036d80","role":"CLAR","role_ordinal":1,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v4"}